			"notes": "TurtleLib 2.0.0 is a breaking release for mod developers: new package names, the MIT license, a reworked update checker, and no more translation helpers. Players only need to update TurtleLib together with the mods that require it.\n\n# Compatibility\n\n- **New packages:** All classes moved from `com.github.hrobasti.turtlelib` to `net.kroet.turtlelib`; mods built for TurtleLib 1.x must be updated and do not run with 2.0.0.\n- **Update together:** Install TurtleLib 2.0.0 only together with mods that require it (e.g. PermaClicker 2.0.0).\n- **Removed helpers:** `LangLoader` and `MessageService` are gone; mods translate with Minecraft's own lang files.\n- **UpdateChecker API:** One constructor with channel, Minecraft version and loader; the result lists the newest release with its link and an error reason per platform.\n\n# New features\n\n- **Core jar:** Every release now includes `TurtleLib_x.y.z_core.jar` for compiling mods against TurtleLib; it is not meant for the `mods/` folder.\n\n# Fixes\n\n- **Version comparison:** A leading `v`, build metadata such as `+26.3` and pre-release numbers such as `beta.2` are now compared correctly.\n- **Update check:** No longer fails when a platform is unreachable, reads CurseForge results correctly and only counts releases for the given loader and Minecraft version.\n- **NeoForge warning:** The \"deprecated logoFile\" warning no longer appears in the NeoForge log.\n\n# Other\n\n- **Mod Menu:** Mod Menu may now check TurtleLib for updates as well.\n- **Mod details:** Updated description, icon and links in Mod Menu and the NeoForge mod list.\n- **MIT license:** TurtleLib is now licensed under MIT (previously Apache-2.0).\n- **Build from source:** The repository now builds on its own, without the development workspace.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/hrobasti/turtle-lib-mod/compare/1.3.0...2.0.0"
		},
